WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.390
Census, 2021.

2
00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:06.660
For the first time, under half the people
of England and Wales call themselves

3
00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:07.720
Christian.

4
00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:10.980
37 per cent say they have no religion.

5
00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:16.180
Back in 1927, Sigmund Freud
called religious ideas illusions,

6
00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:17.960
driven by our wishes.

7
00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:23.180
In 2006, Richard Dawkins chose
a stronger word: delusion.

8
00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:26.240
So is belief in God just wishful thinking?

9
00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:28.940
And would society be happier without it?

10
00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:31.180
In this mission, you'll meet the critics,

11
00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:33.540
and the Christian
thinkers who answer them.

12
00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:38.380
Then you'll weigh up the claim that society
would be happier without Christianity.

13
00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:42.270
Your mission: test the critics'
case, and the replies to it.
